Third-party material

AlbumCraft builds embed the default fonts of egui (crate epaint_default_fonts), used for the user
interface and drawn into pictures by the text effect and print captions:

  Ubuntu Light (Ubuntu-Light.ttf) - Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0
  Hack Regular (Hack-Regular.ttf) - MIT License (Copyright 2018 Source Foundry Authors; DejaVu parts public domain)
  Noto Emoji (NotoEmoji-Regular.ttf) - SIL Open Font License 1.1
  emoji-icon-font / egui-icons (emoji-icon-font.ttf, egui-icons.ttf) - MIT License (Copyright 2014 John Slegers)

Their license texts are in the epaint_default_fonts crate (fonts/UFL.txt, fonts/Hack-Regular.txt,
fonts/OFL.txt, fonts/emoji-icon-font-mit-license.txt).

AlbumCraft builds embed a subset of the Material Symbols icon font (assets/fonts/, Copyright
Google LLC), Apache License 2.0 (assets/fonts/LICENSE-MaterialSymbols).

AlbumCraft builds embed icons of Fluent UI System Icons (assets/icons/, Copyright (c) 2020
Microsoft Corporation), MIT License (assets/icons/LICENSE).

AlbumCraft builds embed map data (assets/geo/, details in assets/geo/README.md):

  Land, lakes and country borders - Natural Earth (naturalearthdata.com), public domain
  World cities (cities15000) - GeoNames (geonames.org), Creative Commons Attribution 4.0

AlbumCraft builds embed the YuNet face detector (crates/albumcraft-ai/networks/, OpenCV Zoo
2023mar, Copyright (c) 2020 Shiqi Yu), MIT License (crates/albumcraft-ai/networks/LICENSE-YuNet);
its input size was made free, nothing else changed (networks/README.md).

When the user turns face grouping on, the SFace face recogniser (OpenCV Zoo 2021dec, Apache
License 2.0) is downloaded from AlbumCraft's own releases; it is not distributed with the program.

When the user turns online maps on, map pictures and place searches come from OpenStreetMap
(© OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License); they are not distributed with AlbumCraft.

AlbumCraft builds with videos use the FFmpeg libraries (ffmpeg.org; libavcodec, libavformat,
libavutil, libswscale, libswresample), GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1 or later, and
dav1d (VideoLAN, BSD 2-Clause License), as separate shared libraries built without FFmpeg's GPL
and non-free parts (packaging/ffmpeg/build.sh, which names the exact source releases). The
packages carry them beside the program with their licence texts (FFmpeg-COPYING.LGPLv2.1,
dav1d-COPYING); they may be replaced with other builds of the same versions.

AlbumCraft builds include ONNX Runtime (Copyright Microsoft Corporation, MIT License), linked in
through the ort crate (pyke.io, MIT OR Apache-2.0), to run the networks of the optional AI
features. The Linux packages carry it as Microsoft's own library file (libonnxruntime.so) with
its licence and third-party notices (LICENSE-ONNXRuntime, ThirdPartyNotices-ONNXRuntime.txt). No network is distributed with AlbumCraft: each is downloaded when the user asks, and
its licence is shown before.

AlbumCraft builds with videos (Cargo feature `video`, on by default) use the FFmpeg libraries
(ffmpeg.org; libavcodec, libavformat, libavutil, libswscale, libswresample), GNU Lesser General
Public License 2.1 or later, and dav1d (VideoLAN, BSD 2-Clause License), loaded as shared
libraries. They are built from their unchanged release sources by packaging/ffmpeg/build.sh,
which says how (decoders and file readers only, no GPL or non-free parts); their licence texts
go with the libraries (share/licenses/). The Rust bindings are the ffmpeg-next and
ffmpeg-sys-next crates (WTFPL).

All other dependencies are Rust crates under their own licenses (see Cargo.lock; most are MIT
and/or Apache-2.0). Movie export runs the separately installed FFmpeg program, which is not
distributed with AlbumCraft.
